<!DOCTYPE html>
<html data-surface="studio" lang="en">
  <head>
    <title><%= content_for(:title) || t("setup.layout.title") %></title>
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
    <%= csrf_meta_tags %>
    <%= csp_meta_tag %>
    <%# turbo-rails' consumer reads the socket's address here and otherwise asks /cable. %>
    <%= action_cable_meta_tag %>
    <%= render "shared/theme_head" %>
    <%= stylesheet_link_tag "tailwind", "data-turbo-track": "reload" %>
    <%# The wizard loads the `application` entry point. The one step that
        shows a token, `mcp_token_created`, asks for `admin` instead
        (`content_for :entry_point`), so the token's copy box and its
        blanking at `pagehide` are CS Studio's own scripts, the AI assistant
        page's, and it puts `turbo-cache-control: no-cache` in `:head`. %>
    <%= javascript_importmap_tags(content_for(:entry_point) == "admin" ? "admin" : "application") %>
    <%= yield :head %>
  </head>

  <%# scheme-light/dark:scheme-dark: native controls and the canvas follow
      the token theme. Scoped to this product layout on purpose -- a global
      color-scheme would restyle the public site for dark-OS visitors.
      The header as on sign-in; below it the step list (`setup/steps`) and,
      28px to its right, the card that holds the step. The words are read by
      full key (`setup.layout.*`): a lazy lookup from a layout lands in
      `layouts.setup.*`. %>
  <body class="min-h-screen bg-paper font-cs text-ink scheme-light dark:scheme-dark">
    <header class="flex items-center justify-between px-7 py-5">
      <%= render "admin/shared/product_wordmark", link: false %>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
        <span class="hidden text-small text-meta sm:inline"><%= t("setup.layout.first_run") %></span>
        <%= render Admin::Ui::ThemeSwitchComponent.new %>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-[980px] gap-7 px-4 pb-16 md:grid-cols-[250px_minmax(0,1fr)]">
      <%= render "setup/steps" %>

      <main class="min-h-[32rem] rounded-rail bg-surface p-6 shadow-2 md:p-11">
        <%# The wizard takes the setup token and the first account's password,
            before anyone is signed in: in production over plain HTTP it says
            so to everyone, as the sign-in page does (the component's own
            rule; nothing is drawn otherwise). %>
        <%= render Admin::Ui::InsecureNoticeComponent.new(request: request, class: "mb-6") %>
        <%= render "setup/flash" %>
        <%= yield %>
      </main>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
